course: dictionary
lesson: 6799
title: What is ore?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ore is rock or earth that has a useful metal hidden inside it, such as iron or copper. People dig it up from the ground. «Rocks with enough metal in them to be worth digging are called ores.»
explain: Ore is not pure metal yet. The metal has to be taken out of the rock first. «Smelting heats ore with fuel such as charcoal or coke to free the metal.» So the ore is the rock, and the metal is what you get after smelting.
explain: Look at the words around ore for clues. Words like iron, copper and gold tell you which metal is hidden inside. To check your meaning, swap in "rock with metal in it" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Ore is rock or earth with a useful metal in it.
fact: Iron ore is heated in a furnace to make iron.
fact: Other examples of ore are copper ore and gold ore.
fact: Smelting heats ore with fuel to free the metal from the rock.
fact: Ore is often mined, which means dug out of the ground.
exercise: «Smelting heats ore with fuel such as charcoal or coke to free the metal.» What is ore in this sentence? | A kind of fuel | Water pumped from a mine | Pure metal ready to use | *Rock with a useful metal inside it
exercise: Which phrase means rock with copper in it? | *Copper ore | Copper sky | Copper cup
exercise: «Recycling metals uses much less energy than mining new ore.» What does this sentence suggest? | Metal cannot be recycled | Ore is made of wood | Recycling uses more energy than mining | *Digging up new ore uses more energy than reusing metal
test: Which of these is dug from the ground? | Wind | Sunlight | *Coal | Air
test: What does smelting do to ore? | Throws it into the sea | Paints it gold | Cools it to make it hard | *Heats it with fuel to free the metal
exam: «Marie Curie separated tiny amounts of new elements from tonnes of ore.» What does this suggest about ore? | Ore floats on water | Ore is soft like sand | *Ore is mostly rock, so huge amounts must be dug for a little metal | Ore is pure gold, so only a small amount is needed
